    <string name="settings_remote">Remote control (Discord)</string>
    <string name="remote_explain">Control the tablet from your phone by posting in a private Discord channel. One-time setup:

1. Go to discord.com/developers/applications and tap New Application.
2. Open Bot (left menu). Tap Reset Token and copy it into \"Bot token\" below. Turn ON \"Message Content Intent\" and save.
3. Open OAuth2 > URL Generator. Under Scopes tick \"bot\". Under Bot Permissions tick View Channels, Send Messages and Read Message History.
4. Open the generated URL at the bottom, pick your server and tap Authorize.
5. In Discord turn on Settings > Advanced > Developer Mode. Long-press your private text channel > Copy Channel ID and paste it below. Make sure the bot can see that channel.
6. Type your Discord user name (or user id) below. Only the people you list are obeyed.
7. Turn the switch on and tap Send a test message.

Then type in that channel: status, usage, settings, lock now, unlock, extend 30, extend until 8:30pm, limit 90, limit off, bedtime 8pm to 7am, bedtime off, reset time, summary now, summary at 9pm, new day at 6am, help.</string>
